// Position matrix (design 235), grid 1 "Adoption" — row: enum raw value,
// sources S6 (qualified/module static read) and S7 (call result). Neither
// is a compile-time constant expression, and the enum raw value position
// refuses BOTH cleanly (no ICE) — the design already documents that a case
// value "may NOT name a `static` or another enum's case" (DF-232c); this
// confirms the same clean refusal covers a function call too, and that the
// refusal is the SAME diagnostic rather than two different failure shapes.
// A local read (S4) and a field read (S5) are structurally impossible to
// write in this position (no enclosing function scope/receiver exists
// inside an enum declaration) — N/A, not tested. A place read (S8, `v[i]`)
// is refused the same way for the same reason (not a constant); not
// independently pinned since it is the identical diagnostic.
//
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: raw value for case `A` of enum `E` is not a compile-time constant
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: may not name a `static` or another enum's case

static N: UInt8 = 5

enum E: UInt8 {
    case A = N,
}

func main() {
    print("{E.A as UInt8}")
}
